# Frontend feature folders

Colocate by **product feature**, not by layer name. A screen, its manager, its API client, and its tests travel together.

## Layout

```text
src/features/<feature>/   api, lib (managers), components, pages, *.test.ts
src/shared/ui             primitives + engines (Modal, PhoneList, shadcn)
src/shared/lib            cross-feature helpers (cn, abilities, structure-tree)
src/shared/api            HTTP core / auth session only
src/shared/layout         shell, sidebar, topbar
src/app                   App.tsx, routes, main.tsx
```

Features: `attendance`, `giving`, `roster`, `events`, `access`, `settings`, `account`, `auth`, `overview`, `notifications`.

## What is shared vs feature

| Shared | Feature |
|--------|---------|
| Used by two+ features with the **same** API | One feature’s screens, adapters, policies |
| Primitive / engine (PhoneList chrome) | Adapter (`membershipPhoneCard`, guest-risk banner) |
| Domain kernel (`structure-tree`, `createUnitPolicy`) | Page + RTK endpoints for that page |

If Church → Cell and Giving → Cell would copy an `if`, that helper is **shared** (or a missing manager) — not a second copy inside giving.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — attendance policy parked in a global dump
// src/lib/guest-risk-warning.ts
// src/lib/phone-list-adapters.ts  (membership + attendance + giving in one file)

// ✅ GOOD
// src/features/attendance/lib/guest-risk-warning.ts
// src/features/roster/lib/membership-phone-card.ts
// src/shared/ui/phone-list.tsx          // engine only
```

## Before adding a file

1. Name the feature. Put the file there (`features/<feature>/…`).
2. If two features need it, move the **engine** to `shared/` and leave adapters in each feature.
3. Do not add new modules under the old flat `src/lib` or `src/pages` — migrate the neighbor when you touch it.
4. Tests sit next to the module. Barrel (`index.ts`) only for the feature’s public exports.

## With other rules

Volatility-decomposition still applies **inside** a feature (manager vs engine). No-god-files still applies (≤400 / 600). A feature folder is not a new dump site.
